course: dictionary
lesson: 4390
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Hail can mean small balls of ice falling from the sky, or it can mean calling out to someone. The words around it tell you which meaning you need.
explain: «Clouds form when moist air rises and cools... when the cloud is cold enough the water falls as snow or hail.» The clues are clouds and falling, so hail is weather here. Now look at «hailing a taxi»: the clue is taxi, so hail means to wave or call out. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Hail can also mean praise. «He was hailed as a hero» means people praised him loudly. Hail from means come from, as in «hails from Ireland». When hail is a noun and you see «a hail of», it means a lot of things arriving at once.
fact: Hail is small balls of ice that fall from storm clouds, like hard rain.
fact: To hail means to call out or wave to get someone's attention, as in hailing a taxi.
fact: Hail is most common in warm-season thunderstorms, not in winter snow.
fact: When big hailstones fall, go indoors and stay away from windows, because hail can hurt people and break glass.
fact: «A hail of arrows» means a lot of arrows coming at once.
exercise: «When the cloud is cold enough, the water falls as snow or hail.» In this sentence, what is hail? | A loud shout to get someone's attention | *Small balls of ice that fall from storm clouds | A flat grey cloud | A warm wind in summer
exercise: «She stood at the kerb and hailed a taxi.» What does hailed mean here? | To come from a place | To praise someone loudly as a hero | *To wave or call out to get someone's attention | To fall from the sky like ice
exercise: «The hail of stones rattled on the roof.» What does a hail of stones mean? | A soft, warm rain | A kind of wall | *A lot of stones coming at once | One small stone on the roof
test: «He was hailed as a hero when he came home.» What does hailed as a hero mean? | *Praised loudly as a hero | Covered in ice | Sent away from home | Shouted at by a crowd
test: «Maya hails from Ireland.» What does hails from mean? | *Comes from Ireland | Is sailing to Ireland | Is scared of Ireland | Is hailing a taxi in Ireland
exam: When big hailstones fall, what should you do, and why? | *Go indoors and stay away from windows, because hail can hurt people and break glass | Open the windows to see the storm better | Stand under a tree and wave to your friends | Run outside and catch the hailstones in a bowl
